(2) false (non-)instances of the guarded named lgg under alpha-variation
   Coll   lgg blocks [(1,), (2,)]     instance of lgg True, guards ok True, sentence True, schema instance False
          ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃x2.x2=x1) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ ¬∀x4.x4=x4)))
   ReplU  lgg blocks [(1,), (2,)]     instance of lgg True, guards ok True, sentence True, schema instance False
          ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃!x2.x2=x1) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ ¬∀x4.x4=x4)))
   ReplS  lgg blocks [(1,), (2,), (3,)] instance of lgg True, guards ok True, sentence True, schema instance False
          ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃x2.(x2=x1 ∧ ∀x3.(¬∀x4.x4=x4 → x3=x2))) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ ¬∀x4.x4=x4)))

(3) Sep, SepJ under alpha-variation: random instances of the guarded lgg are genuine
   Sep   guarded-lgg instances tested 1236, genuine 1236
   SepJ  guarded-lgg instances tested 720, genuine 720

(4) Thm C2(iii) under alpha-variation.  Family s_n = alpha-variant of Coll/ReplU/ReplS(phi_n),
    phi_n = ~^{2n}(y = x & x in A), all binder names distinct; designated leaf: the y of the atom y = x in the
    consequent occurrence (the A-leaf used for de Bruijn is NOT unique here: x in A is also a frame atom).
    (a) Lemma C1 hypothesis: every proper-prefix subterm on the path occurs once;  (b) for every prefix q one
    of TOP/BOT makes s_n[q<-v] imply "every set is empty" in all membership structures of size <= 3.
   Coll   (a) n = 0..6 unique: True   (b) n = 0,1: 20 prefixes, each with a v making s[q<-v] |= "all sets empty": True
   ReplU  (a) n = 0..6 unique: True   (b) n = 0,1: 20 prefixes, each with a v making s[q<-v] |= "all sets empty": True
   ReplS  (a) n = 0..6 unique: True   (b) n = 0,1: 20 prefixes, each with a v making s[q<-v] |= "all sets empty": True
